  "outcome": {
    "status": "rejected",
    "decidedBy": "George Le",
    "decidedAt": "2026-11-20T04:52:36.185Z",
    "quote": "the horizontal stabilizer below the tail is too far set into the tail, the rear landing gear should be pointed to back and have a supporting strut (they form a triangle due to the connection). The front landing gear are lower and also have one leg going straight downward and an angled strut from the front going down at an angle. Both of which should be visible from the side, the front one is visible from the front. The blackhawk body should be flat all the way back with no hump. The cheek windows should be in the forward at the bottom of the nose by the front windows"
  },
